; www.example. is in the zone and has an A.  Ask it for an AAAA and the
; answer is NOERROR with nothing in it, and -- the zone being signed --
; an NSEC saying which types the name does have.
;
; The configuration has the server deny the name instead.  The rcode is
; all that changes: the NSEC still goes out, still signed, still saying
; the name is there.  So the header and the proof below it say different
; things, and only one of them is signed.
;
; other.example. is here to show that the server is otherwise sane and
; that the deviation is exactly one name wide.
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@	IN	SOA	ns.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@	IN	NS	ns.example.
ns	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
www	IN	A	192.0.2.1
other	IN	A	192.0.2.2
